2. Example of the register problem

Consider this illustrative Smali method:

.method public o()[B
    .locals 2

    const/4 v0, 0x0
    const/4 v1, 0x1

    invoke-static {v0, v4}, Lcom/example/Bridge;->process(II)V

    return-object v0
.end method

This is invalid because ".locals 2" provides only "v0" and "v1". The generated invoke references "v4", which does not exist in this register frame.

The example is illustrative, not a claim that this is the exact instruction in the Sentry method.

A valid transformation must calculate the actual register frame and ensure that every referenced register exists.

For example, if the intended operation genuinely requires "v4", the register allocation must reserve sufficient registers and preserve the original values and types:

